  (4
  ("4" 0.1963 0.2046 0.1388 0.1494 0.1494 0.0105 nil nil 0.0084 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 0)
  ("Conor McBride and Ross Paterson" 0.3687 0.6263 0.1388 0.1494 0.1494 0.0105 0.00599 0.2641 0.0456 "SQWLIR+CMTI10" 0.0118 nil t 4)
  ("The idea is that pure embeds pure computations into the pure fragment of an" 0.2038 0.7988 0.1672 0.1777 0.1777 0.0105 0.00757 0.2295 0.0288 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 13)
  ("effectful world—the resulting computations may thus be shunted around freely, as" 0.1963 0.7988 0.1826 0.1931 0.1931 0.0105 0.00571 0.3073 0.0577 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 10)
  ("long as the order of the genuinely effectful computations is preserved." 0.1963 0.7059 0.1980 0.2085 0.2085 0.0105 0.00557 0.2346 0.0307 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 10)
  ("You can easily check that applicative functors are indeed functors, with the fol-" 0.2130 0.7988 0.2135 0.2240 0.2240 0.0105 0.00582 0.2322 0.0288 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 12)
  ("lowing action on functions:" 0.1963 0.3935 0.2289 0.2394 0.2394 0.0105 0.00557 0.2597 0.0469 "NSCVXQ+CMR10" 0.0118 nil nil 3)
